    pr_ref:  # e6a4
    description: "Latent-bug flag from the WI-hiziz PR-2 design memo (wf_6991b0ea-f64) and review. py.py derives an enclosing class short name via caller_symbol.name.split('.')[0] at (formerly) py.py:3816 (an existing idiom predating PR-2). Today a method's name/qualified_name is exactly 'Class.method' (one dot), so [0] == [-2] and both yield the direct class. But the field is only bare-two-segment by current convention; if a future change ever chains the full scope ('Outer.Inner.method'), [0] yields 'Outer' (WRONG) while [-2] yields 'Inner' (the direct enclosing class — the class_ids_by_name key). WI-hiziz PR-2's new Site-1 emission deliberately uses .split('.')[-2] for exactly this robustness. Harmonize the sibling site(s) to [-2] to remove the latent divergence. Pure refactor, no behavior change on the current producer; verify with a nested-class test."  # e6a4
    fields: {}  # e6a4
