  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f. There are now two [0] sites: py.py:7519 (class_name for class_field_types) and py.py:7560 (_own_cls for class_external_field_types, added by a21ef3223f INV-mumov). The qualified_name sites at 9933/10111 already use [-2]. Today a nested-class method is named 'B.go', so the two agree: fixture fx_fazid (A.B.go calling self.c.ping()) resolves to C.ping at 0.85. Latent premise holds; harmonize both sites. It turns into a live bug if WI-naviz chains the full scope into name. MECHANISM: enclosing class derived as name.split('.')[0] (first segment) instead of [-2] (direct owner); correct only while method names are two-segment. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-naviz."  # 3dd7
